    {
      "id": 126642,
      "name": "McBehrer",
      "username": "McBehrer",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mcbehrer/{size}/1850_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-01-11T07:03:04.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Because generally, destroying something immediately ends any effects they had in play; cards with an effect that specifically says \"when this card is destroyed,\" however -- such as any of Akash'Bhuta's limbs, the explosives wagon, etc. -- are a special exception. They remain in play to resolve their effect, but only because they must act after they are destroyed.</p>",
      "post_number": 7,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:01:07.473Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
