      "raw": "[quote=\"Cosmonaut Zero\"]\n\nWhat I&#39;m not understanding is how the same set of basic principles could possibly produce both the Cryo Bot ruling and the Mountainous Carapace ruling.Is it just the case that effects triggered by destruction are an exception to the basic principles, or is there some explanation that works for both that I&#39;m missing?\n\n[/quote]\n\nBeing dealt damage and destruction effects are not the same trigger. Triggers can also interrupt other triggers (note End of Days with Bee Bot). If Cryo Bot is dealt damage, he would typically trigger. However if that damage caused him to go to 0 or fewer HP, a new trigger occurs after he was dealt damage, that being him being 0 or fewer HP. The destruction trigger interrupts the damage trigger, moving Cryo Bot to the trash. You would go be to the being deal trigger, but he is no longer in play, thus not being able to do anything and that&#39;s the end of it.\n",
