    {
      "id": 126644,
      "name": "Cosmonaut Zero",
      "username": "Cosmonaut_Zero",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/cosmonaut_zero/{size}/2520_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-01-12T03:34:09.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>That process makes sense to me. But if the damage and destruction complete before the triggers complete then I don't see how cards with the text, \"When this card is destroyed ...\" do anything at all, not to mention consider themselves to still be in play while they're performing their text. Essentially, I feel like the two diffent triggers can't be following the same timing rules, and I can't identify any basic principles that would make me think they would need to behave differently.</p><p>I have a new solution. When I see \"When this card is destroyed...\" I'm going to mentally substitute \"When this card would be destroyed by any other card .... instead. Then destroy this card.\" That lets the timing rules be self-consistent in my mind and still follow all of the official rulings.</p>",
      "post_number": 9,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:01:07.608Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
