      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>That process makes sense to me. But if the damage and destruction complete before the triggers complete then I don&#39;t see how cards with the text, &quot;When this card is destroyed ...&quot; do anything at all, not to mention consider themselves to still be in play while they&#39;re performing their text. Essentially, I feel like the two diffent triggers can&#39;t be following the same timing rules, and I can&#39;t identify any basic principles that would make me think they would need to behave differently.</p><p>I have a new solution. When I see &quot;When this card is destroyed...&quot; I&#39;m going to mentally substitute &quot;When this card would be destroyed by any other card .... instead. Then destroy this card.&quot; That lets the timing rules be self-consistent in my mind and still follow all of the official rulings.</p>",
