    {
      "id": 126646,
      "name": "AlexxKay",
      "username": "AlexxKay",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/59ef9b/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2015-01-12T04:16:49.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"phantaskippy\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/48/1897_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> phantaskippy:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<ol start=\"3\">\n<li>&nbsp;If destruction is not prevented and after any on destruct text from the card itself is resolved it leaves play, enters the trash and counts as destroyed for \"when ___ is destroyed\" text on other cards.&nbsp;I believe this is the proper order.</li>\n</ol>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Given your claims (and subsequent discussion) <a href=\"https://greaterthangames.com/comment/93918#comment-93918\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">here</a>, I would modify that slightly.</p>\n<ol start=\"3\">\n<li>&nbsp;If destruction is not prevented and after any on destruct text from the card itself is resolved it leaves play, then…</li>\n</ol>\n<p>3a. All destruction triggers <em>not</em> on the destroyed card happen.&nbsp; (I <em>think</em> this includes triggers on \"leaving play\", but am less sure about that.)</p>\n<p>3b. Destroyed card goes to trash (unless it already went somewhere else due to 3a).</p>",
      "post_number": 11,
