    {
      "id": 126647,
      "name": "phantaskippy",
      "username": "phantaskippy",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-01-12T13:38:41.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Good point</p><p>Unforgiving Wasteland can prevent a card's on destruction text,so those kind of triggers (triggers that use instead to cancel destruction) have to go first.</p><p>Triggers that do stuff to put a card somewhere else but do not include \"instead\" and do not prevent destruction would be 3a.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>We have no ruling on shether a card leaving play and being destroyed is equivalent timing in the common destruction where both qualify. &nbsp;I think it would work.</p><p>Will change my post.</p>",
